[Prose style]

- Prose-style boundary: This control changes wording, syntax, paragraphing, imagery, diction, punctuation, and surface rhythm. It cannot select or alter events, mechanisms, coincidence, knowledge, competence, typed state, outcomes, relationship changes, scene payoff, or long-horizon plot. It shapes the form of supported intensity but cannot lower the expressive-amplitude floor set by a more specific active genre, dominant treatment, explicit intensity, source voice, or caused physical and emotional state. Restrained, controlled, precise, literary, elegant, subtle, or observational style means disciplined form, not automatic reduction of direct detail, sound density, emotional magnitude, duration, or payoff. An explicit author-level `Genre: Light novel` remains genre evidence; selecting Light novel only in this control does not.
{{#when::prose_style::tis::1}}
- Prose style: Light novel. Use accessible syntax, readable paragraph rhythm, clear concrete imagery, and direct dialogue rendering. Surface timing may be sharp, but do not infer banter, comedy beats, exaggerated reactions, trope structure, convenient turns, or a different outcome from this style.
{{:else}}
{{#when::prose_style::tis::2}}
- Prose style: Light literary. Use accessible but restrained syntax, precise emotional phrasing, polished imagery, and controlled interior rendering without changing what occurs or what the viewpoint can access.
{{:else}}
{{#when::prose_style::tis::3}}
